# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The web + indexer images are built with `context: .` (see docker-compose.yml),
# so without this file every secret and build artifact in the working tree ends
# up in an intermediate image layer. `.env` in particular is expected to hold
# MAINNET_DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY / MAINNET_RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY / MAINNET_KEEPER_PRIVATE_KEY
# (see .env.example) — it must never reach a layer.

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: dockerignore uses filepath.Match, NOT gitignore semantics — a bare
# `.env` anchors to the context root only. The `**/` prefix is what catches
# apps/web/.env.local (which Next reads at build time) and any other nested
# env file. Do not "simplify" these back to unprefixed patterns.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# --- vcs / tooling -----------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea

# --- dependencies + build output --------------------------------------------
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/out
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo
**/.turbo

# --- foundry / anchor artifacts ---------------------------------------------
packages/contracts/out
packages/contracts/cache
packages/contracts/broadcast
packages/solana-program/target
**/target

# --- audit + planning artifacts ---------------------------------------------
audit
graphify-out
docs/superpowers
docs/sdd
docs/plans
plans
specs
.claude
.cursor
.superpowers
CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.md
*.plan.md
PLAN.md
PLANNING.md
TODO.local.md

# --- misc --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
.DS_Store
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
